<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via $2.5 bln customer RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via $2.5 bln customer RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the U.S. banking system on Wednesday via $2.5 billion customer repurchase agreements, a Fed spokesman said.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the normal time for Fed open market operations, fed funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
